; Requirement: an identification that contradicts a judged difference is
; refused, and the refusal is a result one can read.
;
; egglog's own way to say "these two cannot be merged" is a function with
; :no-merge: two sheets with two inventory names cannot become one sheet.
;
; Observed: the union is refused by aborting the whole run. Exit code 1,
; one line on stderr, and everything printed before it is discarded.

(sort Sheet)
(constructor sheet (String) Sheet)
(function inventory-name (Sheet) String :no-merge)

(set (inventory-name (sheet "a")) "a")
(set (inventory-name (sheet "b")) "b")

(extract "this line is printed before the refusal and never shown")

(union (sheet "a") (sheet "b"))
(run 1)

(extract "never reached")
